  "description": "A builder stands at the edge of a freshly poured slab, knowing that nothing else can go up until this sets. Nobody admires it. Nobody photographs it. But without it, everything above ground eventually falls.\n\nThis sermon sits with one of the most overlooked questions in the Christian life: not what you are building, but what you are building on. Ps Andrew Cartledge works through a claim in 2 Peter that would have sounded scandalous to its original audience, and the implications of that claim reach further than most people expect. There is something here about identity, about the difference between knowing you belong to a family and actually living like you do, and about why the parts of faith that feel the most uncomfortable might be doing the most important work.\n\nWatch this one and let it settle.\n\nBuild.",
